ing on the main EHA Innovation Grant page\\nOur policy on life events\\nOur policy on double awarding\\nYou’ll also need to share our EHA Innovation Grant Agreement Template with your heads of department and institutional representatives. It’s important that these individuals include a statement, in their support letters, that they understand and agree to the conditions in the grant agreement from the outset.\\nPlease note that at this stage you do not need to fill in the grant agreement template or get it signed.\\nEHA Portal account\\nTo apply, you must be registered on the EHA Portal.\\nOnly one principal investigator (PI 1) must submit the application on behalf of the collaboration. However, all PIs must create separate profiles on the EHA Portal and provide personal details.\\nIf you already have an EHA Portal account\\nYou can either:\\nLog in using your existing credentials\\nSelect ‘Reset or create password’ if you cannot remember your details\\nWhen you log in, make sure you use the email address that EHA has on file.\\nIf you do not have an EHA Portal account\\nGo to the EHA Portal and follow the steps under the ‘Create your user profile’ heading.\\nPlease keep in mind that, once you register, it may take\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-8790d2ecdb321c9a833a51f0\", \"title\": \"How to apply for an EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)How to apply for an EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4284, \"end\": 4339, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 55}, {\"start\": 4491, \"end\": 6036, \"excerpt_start\": 56, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n4 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nHow to apply for an EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nBefore you begin\\nMake sure to refer to:\\nThe Bilateral Collaborative Grant Eligibility Checklist to ensure you are eligible\\nMake sure you’ve read and understood:\\nOur policy on life events\\nOur policy on double awarding\\nMake sure you’ve read, understood and agreed to:\\nOur EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant Agreement template. You’ll also need to share with your heads of department and institutional representatives. It’s important that these individuals include a statement, in their support letters, that they understand and agree to the conditions in the grant agreement from the outset.\\nPlease note that at this stage you do not need to fill in the grant agreement template or get it signed.\\nEHA Portal\\nTo apply for an EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant, you should complete the application form on the EHA Portal.\\nOnly one principal investigator (PI 1) must submit the application on behalf of the collaboration. However, both PIs must create separate profiles on the EHA Portal and provide personal details.\\nIf you already have an EHA Portal account, please log in using your existing credentials or select ‘Reset or create password’ if you cannot remember your details.\\nIf you do not have an EHA Portal account, go to the EHA Portal and follow the steps under the ‘Create your user profile’ heading. Registrations are approved from Monday to Friday between 09:00 and 17:00 (Amsterdam time) and it may take up to two business days before your registration is processed. If you submit your\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-81c57feef95692fb83b63747\", \"title\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4082, \"end\": 4115, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 33}, {\"start\": 4184, \"end\": 4239, \"excerpt_start\": 34, \"excerpt_end\": 89}, {\"start\": 4578, \"end\": 6090, \"excerpt_start\": 90, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n3 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nThe call has closed. Winners will be announced by mid-April 2027.\\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grants support collaboration between two independent research groups with complementarity of expertise and showing a mutual need to answer a specific research question.\\nSuccessful applicants can receive up to €320,000 for two years to be divided equally between the two research groups .\\nEligibility\\nYou’re eligible if:\\nBoth principal investigators (PIs) are EHA members\\nBoth PIs are basic and/or translational researchers\\nBoth PIs are independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents\\nThe PIs conduct their research in two different countries in Europe\\nAt least one of the PIs is a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting independent research\\nNote: If an applicant is a physician scientist, at least 50% of their time should be dedicated to lab research\\nUnfortunately, you are not eligible if your proposal relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nTopics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grant’ on your application form.\\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in a country less-represented among EHA grantees, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection proce\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-8696582e313512830ddfba30\", \"title\": \"EHA Innovation Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)EHA Innovation Grant - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4030, \"end\": 4050, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 20}, {\"start\": 4106, \"end\": 4161, \"excerpt_start\": 21, \"excerpt_end\": 76}, {\"start\": 4474, \"end\": 5999, \"excerpt_start\": 77, \"excerpt_end\": 1602}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"EHA Innovation Grant\\nLeft Sidebar\\n4 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nPlease be advised that the call for applications for the 2027 cycle will not open this year. If you would like to be notified when the next application cycle opens, please join our mailing list by contacting us at [email protected].\\nEHA Innovation Grants encourage and support the:\\nCreation of consortia\\nGeneration of preliminary data that can then be used to apply for larger funding opportunities\\nThe grants:\\nSupport high-quality clinical or translational research in hematology\\nLast for a period of two years\\nCan provide a total award of up to €300,000 for the whole consortium\\nEligibility\\nEvery principal investigator (PI) must be an EHA member.\\nAll PIs must be conducting high-quality clinical or translational research. Basic and/or translational researchers can also be included, but the general focus of the project must remain clinical and translational.\\nAll PIs must be independent researchers or group leaders and have full appointments at academic institutes or proven equivalents in Europe.\\nEach consortium must include at least three PIs operating in at least three different countries in Europe.\\nAt least one of the PIs must operate in of the following countries: Albania, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Croatia, Estonia, Georgia, Hungary, Kosovo, Latvia, Lithuania, Moldova, Montenegro, North Macedonia, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Serbia, Slovak Republic, Slovenia, Türkiye, Ukraine.\\nAt least one of the PIs must be a junior independent group leader, within five years of conducting in\"}], \"local_exploration\": {\"visited_doc_ids\": [\"web-307533c1a4508473094316ab\", \"web-f3aba4b966c28f155f997043\", \"web-e00b0a496819dad9ea1b68ec\", \"web-327ebeb04d5b2145598d742a\", \"web-81c57feef95692fb83b63747\", \"web-8696582e313512830ddfba30\", \"web-8790d2ecdb321c9a833a51f0\", \"web-c03ac93bf969f633bdee1f34\"], \"visited_pages\": [{